  <constraints>
    <constraint source="C1 fix direction / CLAUDE.md §11">Scope: implementation shape. ONE implementation of the grant term with Secure suppression, the flag read, the deny-veto resolution and `ApplyVetoPipeline`. The CIAM strategy must reach them through `IAccessibleRecordSetService` (or a method on `AccessibleRecordSetService` both planes call). Copying the pipeline into `CiamContactPrincipalStrategy`, or adding a second veto implementation anywhere, fails this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner model 2026-09-30">Scope: the CIAM term set. CIAM gets the explicit grant term only (direct and organization grants from `GetGrantSetAsync`). It must NOT gain the standing-grant or organization-expansion membership terms. A test pins their absence on CIAM.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner round 2 item 5">Scope: the workforce contact plane. Do NOT remove or narrow its derived-member terms in this task — that would remove "Assigned To *" access before the C9 auto-grant replacement exists. The only permitted difference between the two contact planes after this task is those derived terms, and it must be named in code (one comment at the branch point) and in the task notes, pointing at task 142 escalation (d).</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec FR-21 / owner item 3">Scope: Restricted. On a Restricted record nothing contact-sourced survives on the CIAM plane, whatever the grant level or source (`survivesRestricted` = empty, as on the workforce contact plane, `AccessibleRecordSetService.cs:1296-1301`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec FR-22 / owner item 3">Scope: Secure. On an sprk_issecure root, CIAM rights come ONLY from the contact's own direct grant rows (`DirectAccessLevel`); an organization-inherited grant contributes nothing. Suppression is pre-max and structural, not a post-hoc subtraction (task 037's design crux).</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec FR-23">Scope: No Access List. The deny subject on CIAM is the contact plus its active organizations, read from the SAME single junction read the workforce contact plane uses (`ReadActiveOrgMembershipsAsync`, task 043's single-snapshot invariant). All four key shapes apply (contact×record, contact×org, org×record, org×org). Vetoes run after the max, deny first, then Restricted.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003 / spec NFR-01">Scope: faults. An unreadable root flag is Secure AND Restricted (`RootRecordFlags.Unreadable`, `ExternalCallerContext.cs:149`); an unreadable deny list or subject organization set denies every candidate; nothing on the CIAM plane may fall back to the old grants-only answer when the evaluator faults. A fault must never widen access.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028 A1 / A3">Scope: identity and broker-only. CIAM contact resolution (`ResolveExternalContactAsync`) and its oid-first behaviour are unchanged by this task; all reads stay app-only; no OBO, no Graph types. Handlers stay plane-agnostic — no handler learns which plane it serves.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec NFR-02">Scope: request cost. No per-record round trips: one flag read per root type per composition, one batched deny resolution per composition, one junction read per composition — the same budget as the workforce contact plane.</constraint>
    <constraint source="hot-file coordination">Scope: DI. Do not edit `Infrastructure/DI/ExternalAccessModule.cs`; the strategy's new constructor dependency resolves through the existing scoped registrations (`:177-179`, `:333`). If that proves impossible, escalate rather than editing it (task 134 owns edits there).</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-09-10 / spec">Scope: verification. No Dataverse test in CI. The live check is a MANUAL gate with an existing CIAM test contact and existing non-admin test users in the correct BU; do not propose relocating users. Secure test records are created through the provisioning endpoint, never by editing `sprk_issecure` directly (owner round 2 item 2: the field is locked and endpoint-managed).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests. Plane-parity and veto tests belong at KEEP paths (`tests/integration/seam/ExternalAccess/` for the vertical slice, `tests/unit/.../ExternalAccess/` for the strategy). No `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration tests, no constructor null-check tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this task's PR. Placement decision citing `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`; publish size measured from a FRESH master worktree and a FRESH branch worktree, both at SHORT paths, same Compress-Archive method, equal file counts; report both sizes and the delta; ≤60 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §6.5">Scope: ADR conflicts. If any ADR rule blocks the single-implementation shape, surface it as path A/B/C in the task notes and stop for a decision; never resolve it silently.</constraint>
  </constraints>

