    <outcome date="2026-10-01" branch="task/uac-r2-135" base="task/uac-r2-109-f1" status="code-complete; manual live gate pending; publish size measured by the main session after merge">
      Full record: projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/task-135-ciam-unified-veto-pipeline.md.
      - Fix: IAccessibleRecordSetService gains ComposeForCiamContactAsync(contactId, entityType, ct). It and the
        workforce contact-only path (ComposeForContactAsync) call ONE private ComposeContactPlaneAsync, which holds
        the only contact-plane grant read, junction read, batched flag read, Secure-suppressed grant term, deny
        resolution and ApplyVetoPipeline call. CiamContactPrincipalStrategy keeps identity resolution unchanged and
        maps the evaluator's rights for all three root types; RightsFromGrants is deleted; the strategy reads no
        grant level. ApplyVetoPipeline has exactly two call sites (systemuser path, shared contact path). The false
        parity comment and the CIAM class doc are corrected.
      - Step 1 decision (§11 extend, do not duplicate): refactor the existing contact composition into one core with
        one boolean (includeDerivedMemberTerms); take a contact id, never pass a CIAM caller as a WorkforcePrincipal.
        On CIAM the junction is read after the candidate list and skipped when there are none (systemuser NFR-02 gate).
      - Plane difference: the two derived-member terms stay on the workforce contact plane and stay OFF CIAM. Owner
        decision A2 (round 3, 2026-09-30, binding) answered escalation 3: option (ii), an owner-signed exception.
        Named in one comment at the branch point. Nothing added or retired beyond applying the three rules to CIAM.
      - Escalations: trigger 1 (131) and trigger 2 (109) did not fire — both are on the base. Trigger 3 answered by
        owner A2. Trigger 4 (access removal): READ-ONLY dev comparison, 31 active grant rows, 8 contacts, 14 records,
        0 Restricted / 0 Secure targets, 0 No Access entries => 0 contacts and 0 records change (notes §5). Trigger 5:
